# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Proprietary / per-company content — NEVER push to GitHub
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# NOTE: my-company/ is TRACKED in this repository. This repo is owned by the
# EdgeRunner AI organization and is org-private (explicit collaborators only),
# so the company knowledge base lives in git rather than travelling as
# hand-made snapshot zips. It is still company IP — do not make this repo
# internal or public without moving my-company/ back out first.

# Active and past proposal workspaces: solicitations, customer context,
# drafts, reviews, pricing, teaming strategy — all sensitive.
proposals/

# Customer-targeted demo packets: which customer, what we show them, the talk
# track, and the claim posture. The scenario data inside is synthetic; the
# targeting and the pitch are not. Mirrors check-git-boundary.sh.
demos/

# In-flight proposal workspaces (e.g., working/ussf-sda-rfi/) — same
# rationale as proposals/: drafts, customer-specific content, audit notes.
# (Use working/* + negation so the scaffold .gitkeep can be tracked.)
working/*
!working/.gitkeep

# Calibration corpus per-proposal content — auto-drafts, final submissions,
# edit notes contain real proposal text, customer info, and IP. Keep the
# structure (README + _template) committed but never the per-slug content.
corpus/calibration/*/
!corpus/calibration/_template/

# Personal Claude Code settings (may contain paths, tokens, allow-lists)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Claude Code agent worktrees — created on demand by the bridge, contain
# throwaway branches and per-instance scratch. Never push.
.claude/worktrees/

# Personal editor launch config — contains hardcoded local paths
.claude/launch.json

# HubSpot pipeline scrubs + raw CRM exports — internal deal data, not proposal
# content, but sensitive the same way. Mirrors scripts/check-git-boundary.sh's
# is_sensitive_path() list; keep the two in sync.
scrubs/

# Demand signal register, candidate extracts, and generated briefs. Verbatim
# customer requirements and our own gap admissions, aggregated across every
# pursuit — a worse leak than any single proposal directory. Keep the scaffold
# sentinel so the directory structure survives a fresh clone.
signals/*
!signals/.gitkeep
campaign_rollup.md
watchlist_table.md

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local build artifacts — not source
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Node deps installed inside a proposal (e.g., puppeteer for HTML→PNG)
**/node_modules/

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# .docx renders of review/reference/index markdown — derived artifacts,
# regenerated on demand by scripts/render-md-to-docx.py. Source of truth
# is the .md sibling; don't track the rendered Word doc.
/reference/*.docx
/docs/*.docx
/SKILLS.docx
/SKILL-MERGE-PROPOSAL.docx
/SKILLS-IMPLEMENTATION-*.docx

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OS / editor noise
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# Microsoft Office owner/lock files. Created while a document is open and
# normally removed on close, but they survive a crash or a force-quit and
# then block re-renders and show up in git status.
~$*
.~lock.*#
